## Reviewer points not followed

- uk-a 12 and uk-b 23. A space as the thousands separator is ordinary Ukrainian. This campaign’s checker does not parse it for `uk` (`dot` style). The dotted form was kept. Where the same amount was also called "новий тайванський долар" after TWD, that second name was removed.
- uk-a 14 and uk-b 16. Q16–Q20 are body lines in the Korean source as well, not headings that the Ukrainian file dropped. The U+200B lines in 003, 005, 006, 008, 009, 013 and 015 match that source. Promoting Q16 or deleting the characters fails `headings` or `blocks`.
- uk-a 28. "1,57 млн TWD" is ordinary Ukrainian. A test pins the bytes "TWD 1.57M". The figure was left.
- uk-b 12 and uk-b 22. "кожен учасник має один голос" drops both 1s. Korean "주주 1인 1표" counts two 1s in that paragraph, and Ukrainian has no numeral lexicon entry for "один". The digits stay inside «1 учасник — 1 голос».
- uk-b 17. The English source splits the same sentence across two paragraphs. Merging them changes the block count. Each paragraph was made to stand as its own sentence instead.
- uk-b 19. "не вище розміру фактичної шкоди" alone drops the 1 in Korean "1배". The cap is now "1-кратний розмір", which keeps the digit and does not read as "on one occasion".

Nothing else in the two verdicts looked factually wrong. The case in 010 is about a Korean student; that fact was not generalized. "Найкращі інтереси дитини" is the statutory test and was left.

